WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.370
Redcar and Cleveland,
on Teesside: in 2014,

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.050
a borough of about 135,000 people.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:15.010
In 2014, the borough emitted 8,510
kilotonnes of carbon dioxide equivalent.

4
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:21.670
Two years later, in 2016, the
figure was just 2,192 kilotonnes.

5
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.490
By 2024, it was 672.

6
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.730
So why did nobody in Redcar celebrate?

7
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.210
In this mission, you'll meet the
players who drive economic change:

8
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.390
companies, governments and
international institutions.

9
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.070
Then you'll follow what
came next on Teesside,

10
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.490
from a new development
corporation to a freeport.

11
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:48.350
Your mission: explain why a huge fall in
Redcar's emissions was no reason to celebrate.
